::GEO_U02_L06_GP_Q04::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L06_GP_Q04<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.TRI.3<br><br>Question:<br>Why can valid triangle congruence criteria be connected to rigid transformations? {
= Rigid transformations preserve side lengths and angle measures#Correct. Rigid transformations preserve side lengths and angle measures matches the lesson evidence and supports the mapped standard for this question.
~ Rigid transformations stretch triangles to match#This choice reflects a misconception: Rigid transformations stretch triangles to match. Recheck the given evidence and apply the lesson standard before choosing a conclusion.
~ Rigid transformations prove only similarity#This choice reflects a misconception: Rigid transformations prove only similarity. Recheck the given evidence and apply the lesson standard before choosing a conclusion.
~ Rigid transformations change corresponding parts#This choice reflects a misconception: Rigid transformations change corresponding parts. Recheck the given evidence and apply the lesson standard before choosing a conclusion.
}

